{Winner of the Boyd Best Game Prize} 1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. e3 c5 4. Bd3 d5 5. c3 Nc6 6. Nbd2 Bd6 7. O-O O-O 8. Qe2 e5 9. dxe5 (9. dxc5 $142) 9... Nxe5 10. Nxe5 Bxe5 11. e4 (11. f4 $5 {possibly better}) 11... Qc7 12. h3 Re8 13. Qf3 Be6 14. c4 d4 (14... dxc4 {wins a pawn but allows some counterplay, whereas the text ensures a lasting strongpoint.}) 15. Re1 b5 16. b3 b4 17. Nf1 a5 18. Rb1 a4 19. Qd1 axb3 20. axb3 Ra2 21. Rb2 Rea8 22. Rxa2 Rxa2 23. Bb1 Ra1 24. Qc2 Nh5 {To prevent f2-f4 and take advantage of the weak white light-squared .} 25. Bd2 g6 26. Qd1 Kg7 27. Qf3 Bf4 28. g3 Bxd2 29. Nxd2 Qe5 (29... Bxh3 $2 30. e5) 30. Kg2 Bd7 31. Re2 Ra6 32. Qd3 Qe6 33. h4 Nf6 34. Nf3 Qh3+ 35. Kg1 Ng4 36. Ra2 Rf6 37. Qe2 Rxf3 (37... Rxf3 38. Qxf3 Qh2+ 39. Kf1 Ne5 40. Qf4 Qh1+ 41. Ke2 Bg4+) 0-1

