[Source "Tim Harding"]
[SourceDate "2023.03.21"]
[SourceVersion "3"]
[SourceVersionDate "2023.03.21"]
[SourceQuality "1"]

{I played all three groups in this event (two sets of ten games in this section). Most of the opponents were weak but a draw with Black against the dangerous Franklin was a good result. He scored +7 =2 -1 qualifying for the semifinal in which he beat me. Franklin's other games from the first round do not appear to have been published.} 1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bf4 {Michael was playing the London System long before top GMs took it up. I knew this, of course, and that is why I chose 2...Nc6, holding back the KN development.} Bg4 4. Nbd2 e6 5. c3 Bd6 6. Ne5 Bxe5 7. dxe5 Nge7 8. h3 Bf5 9. g4 Bg6 10. e3 h5 11. Rg1 hxg4 12. hxg4 Nc8 13. Qb3 Nb6 14. a4 a6 15. Nf3 Na5 16. Qb4 Nc6 17. Qb3 Na5 18. Qb4 Nc6 19. Qb3 {Drawn by repetition.} 1/2-1/2

