1. e4 {The new BPCF Open continuous tournament began in the summer of 1985 and Franklin was joint winner with J.C. Wells on 5.5/6 in the first prelininary section (results in IC Sept 1986 p19). He thus qualified for the second semifinal section; the start-list is on p16 of the same IC issue.) J. Lyon won the section and S. Harwood qualified as runner-up ahead of Franklin. Franklin played in several preliminary and semifinal sections between 1985 and about 2001 (by which time BPCF had become BFCC). Franklin played just one Final (F6). Only some games of preliminary and semifinal sections were published in the Information Circular.} c5 2. f4 d5 3. exd5 Qxd5 4. Nc3 Qd8 5. Nf3 Nc6 6. Bb5 Bd7 7. O-O Nf6 8. Ne5 Rc8 9. Qe2 Qc7 10. Bxc6 Bxc6 11. f5 Nd7 12. Nxd7 Qxd7 13. d3 b6 14. Bg5 h5 15. Rae1 f6 16. Bd2 Kf7 17. Kh1 Re8 18. d4 e6 19. fxe6+ Rxe6 20. Qxe6+ Qxe6 21. Rxe6 Kxe6 22. d5+ Bxd5 23. Re1+ Kd6 24. Bf4+ Kc6 25. Re8 g5 26. Rd8 Be6 {BFCC Information Circular Sept 1987 p22} 0-1

