1. d4 {Semifinal 15 started late in 1987 and the start-list was published in the BPCF IC Feb 1988 p29. Franklin probably qualified by winning P69 but the issue where the final result of that section is not in my possession. The earliest issue held by the British Library is 4/1989 where I found this game and the final table (on page 24). Franklin finished fourth with 5/7. E. J. Smith and Walker tied first. The other players were J. Lyon, A. Robertson, M. D. Coughlan, P. A. Wilson and N. Cossins. Also A. Provost who withdrew and his games were cancelled. The Feb 88 IC issue result lists includes Franklin's win over me from P69 but he also qualified for S17 which started soon afterwards so he must have had another qualification.} Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. e3 c5 4. c3 d5 5. Bd3 Nbd7 6. Nbd2 Bd6 7. O-O O-O 8. Re1 Qb6 9. e4 cxd4 10. cxd4 dxe4 11. Nxe4 Nxe4 12. Rxe4 Be7 13. Qe2 Re8 14. Bg5 Bxg5 15. Nxg5 h6 16. Nf3 Nf6 17. Rh4 Bd7 18. Ne5 Rac8 19. Rf4 Red8 20. Rd1 Be8 21. Nc4 Qc7 22. Rxf6 gxf6 23. Qg4+ Kf8 24. Qh4 Ke7 25. Ne3 Qa5 26. d5 Rd6 27. h3 Bd7 28. Ng4 exd5 29. Nxh6 Rb6 30. Qh5 Be6 31. Bf5 Rf8 32. Bxe6 fxe6 33. Qg6 Qc5 34. b3 Kd8 35. Ng8 Rc6 36. g3 Qc2 37. Rd3 Qc1+ {BPCF IC either 4/1989 or 1/90 p15 (not sure which as I was working from a photo taken in the BL)} 0-1

