1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 c5 3. e3 e6 4. Bd3 Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. c3 d5 7. Nbd2 Nc6 8. Qe2 b6 9. Re1 Bb7 10. dxc5 Bxc5 11. h3 Re8 ({Better is} 11... Qc7 {, keeping f7 guarded.}) 12. e4 e5 13. exd5 Nxd5 14. Ne4 Bf8 15. Bg5 f6 $2 {The losing move, opening up the c4-f7 diagonal to his king.} 16. Rad1 $1 fxg5 17. Nfxg5 h6 18. Qh5 $1 Nce7 ({Or} 18... hxg5 19. Nxg5 {with an early mate.}) 19. Qf7+ Kh8 20. Qe6 $1 {Source: Birmingham Mail, 12 January 1991} (20. Qe6 {Only now does Black see} Qc8 21. Nf7+ Kg8 22. Nxh6+ Kh8 23. Qg8+ Nxg8 24. Nf7+ Kh7 25. Neg5#) 1-0

