1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 a6 {TH: The O'Kelly variation was one of Franklin's pet systems but it was unsuited to correspondence play where opponents can consult chess literature including opening manuals. Franklin's opening repertoire was probably one of the reasons why his postal chess results were far below his OTB playing strength.} 3. Nc3 b5 4. d4 cxd4 5. Nxd4 Bb7 6. Bg5 Qc7 7. Bd3 e6 8. O-O Be7 9. Bxe7 Nxe7 10. Qe2 Nbc6 11. Nxc6 Bxc6 12. a3 O-O 13. e5 f5 14. f4 Rf7 15. Qf2 g5 $1 16. Qg3 Rg7 17. fxg5 h6 18. h4 hxg5 19. hxg5 Ng6 20. Rae1 Qd8 21. Rf2 Nf8 (21... Nh8 $142 $1 {idea ...Nf7}) 22. Ne2 Rxg5 23. Qe3 Ng6 24. Nf4 Nxf4 25. Qxf4 Rg4 26. Qh6 Qb6 27. Re3 Rg7 28. c3 Rf8 29. Kf1 Qc5 30. Qf4 Rff7 31. Rh3 Rg6 32. Be2 Rfg7 33. Qh4 Qf8 (33... Bxg2+ $2 34. Rxg2 Rxg2 35. Qh8+ Kf7 36. Bh5+ $18) 34. g3 Rg5 35. Rfh2 f4 36. Qh8+ Kf7 37. Qxf8+ Kxf8 38. Rh8+ Ke7 39. gxf4 Rg1+ 40. Kf2 Rb1 41. Ke3 Re1 (41... Rxb2 $2 42. Bh5 Rxh2 43. Re8#) 42. Kd4 Rf7 43. R8h7 Rxh7 44. Rxh7+ Kd8 45. Rh2 Kc7 46. Bd3 Rg1 47. Rf2 Kb6 48. c4 bxc4 49. Bxc4 Rd1+ 50. Ke3 {BPCF IC Nov 1996 p45; JVS commented "A memorable tussle with a strong player whose result in F6 didn't do him justice." TH: The final table in the August issue of IC shows that of 15 players Franklin finished 13th with 5.5/14 and he was worse in the final position against Walters who withdrew.} 1/2-1/2

